From: mwlaboratories <info@mwlabs.be>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx519: let the supplies settle and reset the sensor after power up

On the OnePlus 6 the main camera powers down after every stream and up
again at the next. Measured with a loop of 25-30 stream starts in one
libcamera process: 8/25 to 15/30 of the starts stopped after 0-4 frames
(the VFE stops seeing frames; no CSID error), and twice the first
register write after power up timed out on the CCI bus. With the sensor
kept powered between the starts (runtime PM forbidden), 0/30 and 0/30.
The IMX371 and IMX376 in the same phone, whose drivers software-reset
the sensor and wait 12 ms before programming it, stall 0/20.

The analogue and core supplies are GPIO load switches without a startup
delay in the device tree, and the driver releases XCLR right after
enabling them. Wait 2 ms for the supplies before starting the clock and
releasing XCLR, and software-reset the sensor (12 ms) before writing the
common registers after a power up.

Status: hypothesis until tested on the OnePlus 6 (compile-tested). The
stall itself and its power-cycle dependence are measured.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx519.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx519.c
index 3c62107..349c6a6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx519.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx519.c
@@ -876,6 +876,16 @@ static const char * const imx519_supply_name[] = {
 #define IMX519_XCLR_MIN_DELAY_US	8000
 #define IMX519_XCLR_DELAY_RANGE_US	1000
 
+/*
+ * Time for the supplies to settle before the clock starts and XCLR goes high.
+ * On the OnePlus 6/6T the analogue and core supplies are GPIO load switches
+ * without a startup delay in the device tree.
+ */
+#define IMX519_SUPPLY_SETTLE_US		2000
+
+/* Time after a software reset before the sensor accepts register writes */
+#define IMX519_SW_RESET_DELAY_US	12000
+
 struct imx519 {
 	struct v4l2_subdev sd;
 	struct media_pad pad[NUM_PADS];
@@ -1359,6 +1369,19 @@ static int imx519_start_streaming(struct imx519 *imx519)
 	int ret;
 
 	if (!imx519->common_regs_written) {
+		/*
+		 * Start from a clean state after power up: without the reset,
+		 * a fraction of the streams started after a power cycle stop
+		 * after a few frames, and the first write sometimes times out.
+		 */
+		ret = cci_write(imx519->regmap, CCS_R_SOFTWARE_RESET, 0x01, NULL);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(&client->dev, "%s failed to reset sensor\n",
+				__func__);
+			return ret;
+		}
+		fsleep(IMX519_SW_RESET_DELAY_US);
+
 		ret = cci_multi_reg_write(imx519->regmap, mode_common_regs,
 					  ARRAY_SIZE(mode_common_regs), NULL);
 		if (ret) {
@@ -1474,6 +1497,8 @@ static int imx519_power_on(struct device *dev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	usleep_range(IMX519_SUPPLY_SETTLE_US, IMX519_SUPPLY_SETTLE_US + 500);
+
 	ret = clk_prepare_enable(imx519->xclk);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(&client->dev, "%s: failed to enable clock\n",
